1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,080
In our class, there are several types of people.

2
00:00:06,540 --> 00:00:10,720
Some are great at cracking jokes, while others support from the sidelines.

3
00:00:11,760 --> 00:00:12,880
Then there's me.

4
00:00:18,960 --> 00:00:21,880
Watching everybody else have fun and holding back my laughter.

5
00:00:22,680 --> 00:00:24,640
Uh-oh, I can't hold it in.

6
00:00:25,480 --> 00:00:27,200
Well, at least Nishi finds us hilarious.

7
00:00:27,760 --> 00:00:28,640
Wait, she does?

8
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:30,100
Don't encourage them.

9
00:00:30,280 --> 00:00:30,960
They suck.

10
00:00:31,140 --> 00:00:32,020
What the hell, dude?

11
00:00:32,080 --> 00:00:32,820
Just facts, bro.

12
00:00:32,840 --> 00:00:34,700
Have some faith in our little duo, why don't you?

13
00:00:34,720 --> 00:00:36,200
You just need to write your own material.

14
00:00:36,680 --> 00:00:37,860
They talk so fast.

15
00:00:38,080 --> 00:00:38,880
I can't keep up.

16
00:00:39,120 --> 00:00:40,040
Oh, the greats.

17
00:00:40,100 --> 00:00:41,200
Okay, I see what you're doing.

18
00:00:41,440 --> 00:00:42,280
Come on, guys.

19
00:00:42,400 --> 00:00:44,000
You know Nishi can't handle you.

20
00:00:44,680 --> 00:00:45,200
Sorry, Nishi.

21
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:45,660
Oh, no.

22
00:00:45,940 --> 00:00:46,740
It's so...

23
00:00:46,740 --> 00:00:48,160
I, uh...

24
00:00:48,160 --> 00:00:48,680
Crap.

25
00:00:48,840 --> 00:00:49,780
I killed the moon.

26
00:00:52,480 --> 00:00:53,960
Well, that was terrifying.

27
00:00:54,500 --> 00:00:55,980
I was ready to be talked to.

28
00:00:55,980 --> 00:00:58,740
Oh, I'm really much happier just listening in.

29
00:00:59,040 --> 00:01:01,980
I guess that's what I get for eavesdropping and laughing like a creep.

30
00:01:02,800 --> 00:01:04,920
Are you going down another shyness spiral?

31
00:01:05,380 --> 00:01:07,340
Oh, I was wondering where you went home.

32
00:01:07,520 --> 00:01:09,160
I had to go grab this book from a friend.

33
00:01:09,440 --> 00:01:10,240
For real, though.

34
00:01:10,360 --> 00:01:12,620
For your sake, I wish you weren't always so on edge.

35
00:01:13,040 --> 00:01:13,640
Me too.

36
00:01:13,640 --> 00:01:18,100
I struggle to understand what people are even saying, but the worst part is figuring out

37
00:01:18,100 --> 00:01:19,140
how to answer them.

38
00:01:19,780 --> 00:01:22,620
Piecing together a natural response feels like taking a test.

39
00:01:22,880 --> 00:01:26,780
All sorts of pictures and ideas pop into my brain, but I can't put them into words.

40
00:01:27,040 --> 00:01:27,860
It's too confusing.

41
00:01:28,240 --> 00:01:29,060
I'm not ready.

42
00:01:29,400 --> 00:01:30,600
But you just did it.

43
00:01:30,980 --> 00:01:32,860
Don't worry about it too much this time, okay?

44
00:01:33,320 --> 00:01:36,340
I'd say that conversation's more about the energy than the words.

45
00:01:36,680 --> 00:01:38,180
I appreciate that.

46
00:01:38,180 --> 00:01:41,280
I tend to get extra anxious when it's boys talking.

47
00:01:41,520 --> 00:01:45,140
Whether it's a guy or a girl, both will bleed the same color of red if you stab them.

48
00:01:45,160 --> 00:01:46,500
Please don't test that out.

49
00:01:47,200 --> 00:01:50,360
Speaking of boys, there's one I keep finding myself thinking about.

50
00:01:50,700 --> 00:01:51,540
Are you serious?

51
00:01:51,800 --> 00:01:52,360
Who is it?

52
00:01:52,480 --> 00:01:53,240
You gotta tell me everything.

53
00:01:54,300 --> 00:01:55,580
I found the class next door.

54
00:01:55,880 --> 00:01:56,180
Tani.

55
00:01:59,180 --> 00:01:59,620
Who?

56
00:02:00,800 --> 00:02:01,100
Oh.

57
00:02:01,700 --> 00:02:03,060
Is that the guy from the library?

58
00:02:03,280 --> 00:02:04,100
The one who works with you?

59
00:02:04,100 --> 00:02:04,620
That's him.

60
00:02:04,620 --> 00:02:07,300
If I remember right, you said he doesn't talk much.

61
00:02:07,500 --> 00:02:09,860
Yeah, he keeps to himself for the most part.

62
00:02:10,300 --> 00:02:11,620
But one day...

63
00:02:11,620 --> 00:02:14,100
I'm so bored.

64
00:02:19,620 --> 00:02:20,140
Huh?

65
00:02:21,080 --> 00:02:23,240
I've never seen her in here before.

66
00:02:25,360 --> 00:02:25,840
Hello?

67
00:02:26,300 --> 00:02:26,740
Suzuki?

68
00:02:28,120 --> 00:02:29,360
They know each other?

69
00:02:34,620 --> 00:02:44,480
Something is definitely going on between those two.

70
00:02:44,840 --> 00:02:46,280
And that's why he was on your mind?

71
00:02:46,380 --> 00:02:49,500
Well, I thought Tani was like me, so I was shocked he could find someone.

72
00:02:49,720 --> 00:02:52,360
Well, being a quiet person isn't the same thing as being shy.

73
00:02:52,800 --> 00:02:53,540
Also shocked?

74
00:02:53,840 --> 00:02:54,140
Really?

75
00:02:54,800 --> 00:02:55,480
There's more!

76
00:02:56,020 --> 00:02:59,340
Not only is he dating her, her delinquent friends seem to love him.

77
00:03:00,040 --> 00:03:00,380
Huh.

78
00:03:00,380 --> 00:03:03,800
He wasn't scared if they were pretending to be like them, either.

79
00:03:03,980 --> 00:03:05,500
When he spoke, he was so nonchalant.

80
00:03:05,600 --> 00:03:07,340
It seemed like he was actually having fun!

81
00:03:08,140 --> 00:03:08,500
Hmm.

82
00:03:08,860 --> 00:03:11,060
So he magically got cool like in a movie?

83
00:03:11,260 --> 00:03:13,680
For a quiet guy, he had such funny comebacks.

84
00:03:14,020 --> 00:03:14,960
I couldn't hold it in.

85
00:03:15,100 --> 00:03:18,200
So you were smiling to yourself and fighting back laughter like always.

86
00:03:18,460 --> 00:03:20,120
It would be easier if you could join in, Nish.

87
00:03:20,500 --> 00:03:21,920
I don't want to purchase a movie.

88
00:03:22,280 --> 00:03:23,140
Well, you say that.

89
00:03:23,240 --> 00:03:25,620
But this Tani situation clearly left an impact.

90
00:03:25,760 --> 00:03:26,380
Maybe you're jealous.

91
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:29,480
You should just try talking some more like he's been doing.

92
00:03:29,480 --> 00:03:29,840
Huh?

93
00:03:30,380 --> 00:03:31,800
I wish.

94
00:03:32,160 --> 00:03:33,040
Wait, I am jealous.

95
00:03:33,380 --> 00:03:34,220
Am I turning green?

96
00:03:34,380 --> 00:03:35,440
Foundation will cover it.

97
00:03:36,140 --> 00:03:36,440
Why?

98
00:03:36,440 --> 00:03:36,740
I wish.

99
00:03:37,440 --> 00:03:38,360
Yes, yes, yes, yes, yes.

100
00:03:38,960 --> 00:03:39,380
I wish.

101
00:03:39,440 --> 00:03:52,800
But the Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of Of

102
00:03:52,800 --> 00:04:22,780
1, 4, 4, 5, 6, 7, 3, 4, 2, 1.

103
00:04:22,800 --> 00:04:40,420
Family night

104
00:04:40,420 --> 00:04:42,680
Make a sound loss!

105
00:04:43,200 --> 00:04:46,260
Connect yourself in to your limits

106
00:04:46,260 --> 00:04:48,460
Love was running forward

107
00:04:49,080 --> 00:04:52,180
I'm doing that while we're not waiting for children

108
00:04:52,260 --> 00:04:55,280
Don't last last words

109
00:04:55,300 --> 00:04:57,060
I wanna say muito

110
00:04:58,020 --> 00:05:00,780
The speaking idi��, but first

111
00:05:00,860 --> 00:05:04,420
All this time I thought I wanted to comment

112
00:05:04,420 --> 00:05:11,420
All this time, I thought I wanted to conquer my shyness.

113
00:05:12,180 --> 00:05:15,380
But in reality, maybe I just wanted to be part of the madness.

114
00:05:16,920 --> 00:05:17,760
Then again.

115
00:05:19,500 --> 00:05:20,280
Make sense?

116
00:05:20,520 --> 00:05:21,500
You're a bomb tutor!

117
00:05:21,580 --> 00:05:22,140
Thanks, bro!

118
00:05:22,520 --> 00:05:23,160
They're listening!

119
00:05:23,180 --> 00:05:25,300
Wait, we should be roomies when we go to Yutokyo!

120
00:05:25,620 --> 00:05:27,060
Let's not get ahead of ourselves.

121
00:05:32,100 --> 00:05:33,100
He heard me.

122
00:05:33,420 --> 00:05:34,320
What do I do?

123
00:05:34,420 --> 00:05:35,500
It should have been quieter.

124
00:05:35,860 --> 00:05:37,400
I'm afraid I have no comment.

125
00:05:38,820 --> 00:05:40,380
He's tearing right at me!

126
00:05:40,960 --> 00:05:41,900
Please forgive me!

127
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:43,320
I shouldn't have listened without permission!

128
00:05:43,520 --> 00:05:44,700
I promise I'll never even stop again!

129
00:05:44,900 --> 00:05:45,560
Please don't look at me!

130
00:05:45,600 --> 00:05:46,060
I'm scared!

131
00:05:46,640 --> 00:05:47,400
There's no way.

132
00:05:47,580 --> 00:05:48,340
I can hear it now.

133
00:05:48,720 --> 00:05:50,620
Hey, why are you listening into our conversation?

134
00:05:50,820 --> 00:05:51,540
Who even are you?

135
00:05:51,600 --> 00:05:52,620
What's your problem, freak?

136
00:05:53,160 --> 00:05:54,760
And they would be so valid for that!

137
00:05:54,860 --> 00:05:55,840
I'm a terrible person!

138
00:05:56,740 --> 00:05:58,300
You pack anything good for lunch today?

139
00:05:58,920 --> 00:06:01,660
Are you okay, Niche?

140
00:06:01,660 --> 00:06:08,020
I've been thinking about it, and I'm fine like this.

141
00:06:08,140 --> 00:06:10,280
Being alone is better than embarrassing myself.

142
00:06:10,500 --> 00:06:11,700
What a tortured mind.

143
00:06:11,880 --> 00:06:12,340
Yo, Honda!

144
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:13,640
Hi, Yamada!

145
00:06:14,800 --> 00:06:15,000
Huh?

146
00:06:15,800 --> 00:06:15,960
Hm?

147
00:06:15,960 --> 00:06:18,060
Oh, m'lady.

148
00:06:19,260 --> 00:06:19,660
Meh.

149
00:06:21,520 --> 00:06:23,040
That was an awful response.

150
00:06:23,260 --> 00:06:25,040
Hey, I'm gonna need that book for next period.

151
00:06:25,440 --> 00:06:27,760
I meant to give it back earlier, but I completely forgot.

152
00:06:28,180 --> 00:06:28,760
Here you go.

153
00:06:28,880 --> 00:06:29,540
Wait a sec.

154
00:06:29,680 --> 00:06:31,000
Him and Ho know each other?

155
00:06:32,140 --> 00:06:32,380
Hm?

156
00:06:33,100 --> 00:06:33,280
Huh?

157
00:06:34,860 --> 00:06:35,160
Hm?

158
00:06:35,160 --> 00:06:37,300
Oh, you collect those?

159
00:06:37,600 --> 00:06:37,860
Hm?

160
00:06:39,500 --> 00:06:42,980
I used to collect them, too, but then it got way too hard for my stomach to keep up.

161
00:06:43,280 --> 00:06:44,100
I was corned, though.

162
00:06:44,380 --> 00:06:44,600
Hm.

163
00:06:45,260 --> 00:06:45,540
Yeah.

164
00:06:46,120 --> 00:06:47,480
Which prize were you after?

165
00:06:47,720 --> 00:06:48,180
The Yeti.

166
00:06:48,320 --> 00:06:48,780
Are you five?

167
00:06:49,240 --> 00:06:50,240
Whatever, it's awesome.

168
00:06:50,580 --> 00:06:51,280
So are you a collector?

169
00:06:51,720 --> 00:06:53,080
Like, is your household Yeti?

170
00:06:53,320 --> 00:06:54,220
Yes, what are these questions?

171
00:06:57,500 --> 00:06:59,740
Sorry for laughing at the worst person alive.

172
00:06:59,740 --> 00:07:00,000
Yeah!

173
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:00,060
Yeah!

174
00:07:00,760 --> 00:07:01,100
Oh!

175
00:07:01,700 --> 00:07:02,100
Hurry!

176
00:07:02,360 --> 00:07:03,200
There's a dragonfly!

177
00:07:03,280 --> 00:07:04,040
Rain-paging for our glasses!

178
00:07:04,040 --> 00:07:04,780
Oh, jeez!

179
00:07:04,840 --> 00:07:06,100
You sound like it's eating someone!

180
00:07:06,180 --> 00:07:07,160
Well, time to dilly-dally, girl!

181
00:07:07,160 --> 00:07:07,900
See y'all later!

182
00:07:08,160 --> 00:07:08,840
See ya!

183
00:07:10,320 --> 00:07:11,200
That's the girl!

184
00:07:11,560 --> 00:07:12,940
Sorry I crashed the convo.

185
00:07:13,380 --> 00:07:14,140
Now get up!

186
00:07:14,620 --> 00:07:16,940
Well, you didn't seem too sorry when you summoned me.

187
00:07:16,960 --> 00:07:20,160
Also, dude, who's that girl you were chatting with?

188
00:07:20,400 --> 00:07:20,520
Oh?

189
00:07:20,640 --> 00:07:21,260
Haven't been yet.

190
00:07:21,780 --> 00:07:22,920
You should try it and find out.

191
00:07:24,940 --> 00:07:27,040
She looks like a porcelain doll!

192
00:07:27,340 --> 00:07:28,440
Soup's pretty, huh?

193
00:07:28,740 --> 00:07:28,940
Hm.

194
00:07:30,120 --> 00:07:30,820
She's cute.

195
00:07:31,140 --> 00:07:33,940
Wearing your heart on your sleeve wins you major risk points.

196
00:07:34,040 --> 00:07:34,540
For real?

197
00:07:34,760 --> 00:07:35,140
Yay!

198
00:07:35,320 --> 00:07:36,760
And he catches bugs, too.

199
00:07:37,080 --> 00:07:38,060
Now I feel exploited.

200
00:07:39,340 --> 00:07:41,640
Wait, Yamada was one of the delinquents you mentioned?

201
00:07:41,940 --> 00:07:45,020
We were in the same class before and he's always been super nice.

202
00:07:45,240 --> 00:07:46,640
Oh, that's a relief.

203
00:07:47,100 --> 00:07:50,180
You wouldn't ask some punk to help you catch bugs, would you?

204
00:07:50,280 --> 00:07:51,180
Probably not.

205
00:07:52,540 --> 00:07:52,980
Yeah!

206
00:07:52,980 --> 00:07:55,940
This right here is Yamada.

207
00:07:59,160 --> 00:08:01,740
He's a chill guy but has some trouble knowing himself.

208
00:08:02,160 --> 00:08:03,880
Come on, let me show you what I mean.

209
00:08:05,260 --> 00:08:07,180
He's always had a phone quirk.

210
00:08:07,780 --> 00:08:08,580
Squat and me.

211
00:08:08,580 --> 00:08:13,580
Why are there such stinky losers?

212
00:08:14,200 --> 00:08:15,920
Wrap it up before teacher gets back!

213
00:08:21,640 --> 00:08:25,160
Whenever he hears an unexpected giggle, he has a warm fuzzy attack!

214
00:08:25,160 --> 00:08:26,300
Ha ha ha!

215
00:08:26,380 --> 00:08:26,740
Ha ha ha!

216
00:08:29,600 --> 00:08:31,920
The more different from him the surprise giggler is.

217
00:08:32,580 --> 00:08:33,880
Look at me, look at me, look at me, look at me.

218
00:08:34,280 --> 00:08:35,360
Look at me in my heart, look at me.

219
00:08:35,600 --> 00:08:36,960
I say to my heart, dude.

220
00:08:38,220 --> 00:08:39,240
She laughed.

221
00:08:39,640 --> 00:08:42,920
The happier he gets when the ice melts and a new connection blooms.

222
00:08:43,340 --> 00:08:46,680
He loves it so much the person clings to his brain like an icicle.

223
00:08:47,680 --> 00:08:50,560
Yamada's head is too full of snow to pick up on this trend.

224
00:08:50,900 --> 00:08:51,580
In the library.

225
00:08:51,580 --> 00:08:53,580
Let's not get ahead of ourselves.

226
00:08:54,580 --> 00:08:56,580
Are you hitting on him at a bar?

227
00:08:58,580 --> 00:08:59,580
In the classroom.

228
00:09:02,580 --> 00:09:04,580
That's three whole giggers!

229
00:09:06,580 --> 00:09:08,580
Yeah. Cute.

230
00:09:09,580 --> 00:09:13,580
Your mother thinks she's as sweet as a snow cone, and that's a stone-cold fact.

231
00:09:15,580 --> 00:09:20,580
Maybe it's just a coincidence, but he's been visiting our classroom a lot lately.

232
00:09:21,580 --> 00:09:22,580
Why?

233
00:09:22,580 --> 00:09:23,580
Oh, so you're insane!

234
00:09:24,580 --> 00:09:26,580
You're talking so much!

235
00:09:26,580 --> 00:09:28,580
Ellie's home seems to be having fun!

236
00:09:28,580 --> 00:09:30,580
What music do you like, Nishi?

237
00:09:30,580 --> 00:09:32,580
Um, I don't listen to music.

238
00:09:32,580 --> 00:09:34,580
I do, but it's always old stuff.

239
00:09:34,580 --> 00:09:35,580
I don't know.

240
00:09:36,580 --> 00:09:37,580
Oh, really?

241
00:09:37,580 --> 00:09:39,580
Even the most basic of topics are too much.

242
00:09:39,580 --> 00:09:42,580
It's nice of Yamada to include me in their conversation,

243
00:09:42,580 --> 00:09:46,580
but every time I open my mouth it only highlights how horribly hopeless I am!

244
00:09:46,580 --> 00:09:51,580
Pull it together, Nishi. You got this!

245
00:09:51,580 --> 00:09:54,580
When you're talking to Yamada, there's zero subtext.

246
00:09:54,580 --> 00:09:56,580
He's the perfect practice partner.

247
00:09:56,580 --> 00:09:57,580
Yamada fun!

248
00:09:57,580 --> 00:09:59,580
It's generally a good treat, but come on!

249
00:09:59,580 --> 00:10:02,580
It's painfully obvious he's only here for Nishi.

250
00:10:02,580 --> 00:10:05,580
But they don't know each other, so he's using me as a gateway friend,

251
00:10:05,580 --> 00:10:08,580
and he thinks he's being subtle.

252
00:10:08,580 --> 00:10:10,580
I'm trying to pretend I don't notice,

253
00:10:10,580 --> 00:10:14,580
but between his awkwardness and her cluelessness, it's too much!

254
00:10:14,580 --> 00:10:15,580
Here, for you.

255
00:10:16,580 --> 00:10:18,580
Oh, oh, thanks.

256
00:10:18,580 --> 00:10:20,580
No, stop giving her those!

257
00:10:20,580 --> 00:10:22,580
Just because you can't figure out her interests

258
00:10:22,580 --> 00:10:24,580
doesn't mean you should resort to bread stickers!

259
00:10:24,580 --> 00:10:27,580
It's like when you mention loving something in front of your grandparents

260
00:10:27,580 --> 00:10:30,580
and it becomes your birthday present until the end of time.

261
00:10:30,580 --> 00:10:31,580
Oh, poor Nishi.

262
00:10:31,580 --> 00:10:32,580
What do I do?

263
00:10:32,580 --> 00:10:35,580
I just like the bread that happens to come with stickers.

264
00:10:35,580 --> 00:10:38,580
There's no way I'll have enough by the deadline, but I don't really care.

265
00:10:38,580 --> 00:10:40,580
What do I say now?

266
00:10:40,580 --> 00:10:41,580
That's what her face says!

267
00:10:41,580 --> 00:10:42,580
Later.

268
00:10:42,580 --> 00:10:43,580
Bye.

269
00:10:44,580 --> 00:10:46,580
You get along so well.

270
00:10:46,580 --> 00:10:48,580
Just listening to you is more than enough fun for me.

271
00:10:48,580 --> 00:10:50,580
You've got it all wrong, Nish.

